      "name": "LookupHashTableEntry",
      "signature": "int LookupHashTableEntry(void * pszKey)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Searches a hash table for a string entry with timestamp validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute hash of input string using ComputeStringHash\n2. Get current tick count via GetTickCount\n3. Traverse linked list starting at global g_pHashTableHead\n4. For each node, compare hash value at offset 0\n5. If hash matches, verify timestamp at offset 8 <= current time\n6. Return value at offset 4 if found, 0 if not found or time expired\n\nParameters:\nlpszKey - String to look up in hash table\n\nReturns:\nint - Hash table value if entry found and not expired, 0 otherwise\n\nStructure Layout (Hash Table Node):\nOffset 0x0 (4 bytes): Hash value (uint)\nOffset 0x4 (4 bytes): Result value (int)\nOffset 0x8 (4 bytes): Expiration tick count (uint)\nOffset 0xC (4 bytes): Next node pointer (uint *)\n\nGlobal Data:\ng_pHashTableHead - Head of hash table linked list (uint *)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:6352f0c3f903fb48da2f7f55762422c8",
