      "name": "ClearHashTableAndCleanup",
      "signature": "void ClearHashTableAndCleanup(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Deallocates all hash table nodes and resets the global hash table head pointer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global hash table head pointer (g_pHashTableHead at 0x6fa97630)\n2. If pointer is NULL, skip to cleanup (jump to 0x6fa71fdd)\n3. Iterate through linked list:\n   - Load data pointer from node offset +4\n   - Load next pointer from node offset +0xc\n   - Free data block with SMemFree\n   - Free node structure with SMemFree\n   - Continue with next node\n4. When list is exhausted (next pointer is NULL), exit loop\n5. Clear global pointer to NULL\n6. Call FUN_6fa7b520 for additional cleanup\n7. Return\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles empty list (g_pHashTableHead is NULL)\n- Linked list nodes have embedded pointers: data at +4, next at +0xc\n- Both data block and node structure are freed\n\nStructure Layout (Hash Table Node):\nOffset  Size  Field         Type        Description\n0x0     4     (unused)      uint        Reserved/unused\n0x4     4     pData         void*       Pointer to data block to free\n0x8     4     (unused)      uint        Reserved/unused\n0xc     4     pNext         void*       Pointer to next node\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x108 - Size parameter for first SMemFree call (data block)\n0x109 - Size parameter for second SMemFree call (node structure)\n0x6fa8f20c - Source file string for SMemFree (D2Launcher source reference)\n\nError Handling:\nNo error checking - assumes valid linked list structure\n\nRelated Functions:\nSMemFree - Memory deallocation function\nFUN_6fa7b520 - Additional cleanup routine called after list deallocation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
