      "name": "ReleaseCurrentUnitData",
      "signature": "void ReleaseCurrentUnitData(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Releases the current unit data and its associated composite unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if g_pCurrentUnitData is valid (non-NULL)\n  2. Check composite unit ownership flag at offset 0x1b4 (436)\n  3. If ownership flag is 0, release composite unit at offset 0x1b8 (440)\n  4. Call ReleasePoolAllocation to free unit data (size 0x29c / 668 bytes)\n  5. Clear g_pCurrentUnitData to NULL\n\nParameters:\n  None (uses global g_pCurrentUnitData)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nStructure Layout (offsets accessed from g_pCurrentUnitData):\n  Offset  Size  Field                 Type            Description\n  0x1b4   4     dwCompositeUnitOwned  int             Ownership flag (0=release needed)\n  0x1b8   4     pCompositeUnit        CompositeUnit*  Pointer to composite unit\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns immediately if g_pCurrentUnitData is NULL\n  - Composite unit only released when ownership flag is 0 (not owned elsewhere)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:9388c10cb6694c3d101542e2791f3e48",
