      "name": "ProcessSaveFiles",
      "signature": "undefined4 ProcessSaveFiles(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes all save files in the save directory and loads them into game state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize global save file counter (g_dwSaveFileCount) to 0\n2. Get path to the save directory via GetSaveDirectoryPath()\n3. Build file search pattern using FUN_6fa8547c() with template \"%s\\%s\\*.d2s\"\n4. Open directory search handle via FindFirstFileA()\n5. If no files found (handle == INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE), return 1\n6. For each file enumerated:\n   - Extract filename without extension (copy bytes until '.' delimiter)\n   - Null-terminate extracted filename at g_szSaveFileName\n   - Calculate filename length using SCASB repne instruction (strlen equivalent)\n   - Validate filename:\n     * Length must be in range [2, 15] characters\n     * Character at offset (length - 1) must not be '-'\n     * First character must not be '_'\n   - Call FUN_6fa84da0() to validate file format/integrity\n   - If validation succeeds:\n     * Call FUN_6fa734b0() to load save file into game state with timestamp\n     * Increment g_dwSaveFileCount\n   - Call FindNextFileA() to continue enumeration\n7. After last file or break, close search handle via FindClose()\n8. Return 1 (always success)\n\nParameters:\n   None\n\nReturns:\n   1 - Success (always, even on empty directory)\n\nRemarks:\n   - Only processes D2S save files matching *.d2s pattern\n   - Skips files with invalid filenames (length, starting chars)\n   - Uses stack buffers:\n     * local_400 (1024 bytes) - search pattern path\n     * local_800 (1024 bytes) - save directory path\n     * local_a40 (536 bytes) - WIN32_FIND_DATAA structure\n     * local_900 (256 bytes) - temporary buffer for processing\n   - Global data used:\n     * g_dwSaveFileCount - count of valid save files found\n     * g_szSaveFileName - temporary buffer for extracted filename\n     * g_szSaveFileNamePrev - previous filename for comparison\n   - Calling convention: __stdcall (standard C)\n   - Registers preserved: EBP, ESI, EDI (callee-saved)\n\nNote: Some local variables (cVar1, puVar2, uVar5, iVar3, BVar4) are assembly-only\ntemporaries optimized away during decompilation and cannot be typed individually.",
