      "name": "CreatePlayerGameUnit",
      "signature": "dword CreatePlayerGameUnit(char * pszCharacterName, char * pszRealmName, int nCharacterData, dword dwGameId, dword dwAccountId)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a game unit for a logged-in player character.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Allocate 464-byte game unit structure\\n2. Store character name, realm name, game ID, and account ID\\n3. Decode character attributes from binary format (class, experience, level)\\n4. If first call: initialize realm strings by converting to Unicode format (Diablo realm names)\\n5. Match realm string against known realm list (Normal, FatRealm, BetaWest, BetaEurope, BetaUSWest, BetaUSEast, BetaAsia)\\n6. If match found: apply UI conversion and invoke handler, then return early\\n7. Parse character appearance data: appearance indices (11 bytes), appearance values (16 bytes)\\n8. Parse character attributes: level (byte), life/mana (ushort), resistances (3 bytes), serial (3 bytes)\\n9. Determine unit display type based on character class and attributes\\n10. Create composite unit with specified type, appearance data, and component indices\\n11. If creation fails: clear appearance and retry with fallback class 7 (fallback appearance)\\n12. Configure composite unit with emblem icon, scaled values, and composite mode\\n13. Insert unit into sorted player unit list (sorted by game ID then account ID, or append if expansion)\\n14. Update connection state based on character flags\\n\\nParameters:\\n  pszCharacterName: Null-terminated character name string\\n  pszRealmName: Realm name or NULL (if null, use empty string)\\n  nCharacterData: Pointer to 6+ byte character attribute block\\n  dwGameId: Game ID for unit list sorting\\n  dwAccountId: Account ID for unit list sorting\\n\\nReturns:\\n  1: Unit created and added to list successfully\\n  0: Realm matched special UI handler (early return)\\\"",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
