      "name": "CheckExpansionAndDispatchHandlers",
      "signature": "uint CheckExpansionAndDispatchHandlers(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Checks for expansion MPQ availability and dispatches pending control handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call CheckExpansionMpqExists() to verify expansion data is accessible\n2. If expansion exists (return value non-zero), invoke DispatchPendingControlHandlers()\n3. Return success status (constant 1)\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nuint - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handler dispatch is conditional on expansion availability\n- Return value is always 1 regardless of handler dispatch outcome\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- Return value 1: Indicates successful completion\n\nError Handling:\n- No explicit error handling; silently skips handler dispatch if expansion unavailable\n\nDependencies:\n- CheckExpansionMpqExists: Validates expansion MPQ presence\n- DispatchPendingControlHandlers: Processes queued UI/input events",
