      "name": "LoadGamePlayerData",
      "signature": "void LoadGamePlayerData(char * szDifficultyName, char * pPlayerStructure, dword dwCreateFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Loads and initializes player game data for a difficulty level.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract player slot limit from input structure (offset +7)\n2. Get pointer to first character name in packed string table (offset +9)\n3. Validate expansion MPQ files exist\n4. If expansion not found, validate error message string IDs based on game state\n5. Validate player count string ID matches current game state\n6. Copy global player count to player name count\n7. Load localized UI strings using FUN_6fa761b0\n8. Iterate through each player difficulty slot (min of slot limit vs character count)\n9. For each slot, parse difficulty name and character name strings\n10. Create player game unit with CreatePlayerGameUnit function\n11. If unit creation fails, free all previously allocated hash table entries\n12. Reset hash table head and call cleanup routine FUN_6fa7b520\n13. Check final state and set state change flag if needed\n14. Update game UI state\n\nParameters:\nszDifficultyName (ECX): Pointer to difficulty name string (used as hash key)\npPlayerStructure (EDX): Pointer to player data structure containing:\n  +0x1: ushort - player count (valid players)\n  +0x3: ushort - character count (max slots)\n  +0x7: ushort - player slot limit\n  +0x9: char* - start of packed character name strings\ndwCreateFlags (Stack[0x4]): Creation flags (0=validate, non-zero=create units)\n\nReturns: void\n\nError Handling:\n- Clears dwCreateFlags to 0 on CreatePlayerGameUnit failure\n- Frees entire hash table on failure\n- Calls state reset routine on unit creation error",
