      "comment": "Initializes the gameplay screen and loads character data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear and initialize all game state counters (player count, melee units, etc.)\n2. Load UI control references (character list, expansion features, scrollbar)\n3. Initialize character selection slots with expansion state\n4. Load realm/character selection and determine if entering game\n5. If entering game:\n   - If single player (state==1): Hash character data and load from cache if available\n   - If multiplayer (state!=1): Release old units and enumerate saved character files\n   - Create player units for valid save files\n6. Update UI display and initialize music\n7. Show character selection list\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void (always succeeds, UI updated in place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- File enumeration copies filenames up to first dot or max length\n- Character file validation checks name length (2-16 chars) and exclusions\n- Loop bounds calculated as index/2 for character pairing\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xa0-0xa6, 0x8b, 0x83: UI control indices\n0x5524, 0x58ca: Button field magic values\n0x1419, 0x141a, 0x141b: String IDs for no-expansion message\n0x14e3: Disconnect message string ID\n0x489: Unknown code parameter (ReleasePoolAllocation)\n0x29c: Unknown code parameter (ReleasePoolAllocation)\n\nError Handling:\n- FindFirstFileA returns 0xffffffff on failure (caught with JZ)\n- Realm/character load failure shows disconnect message\n- No expansion MPQ shows appropriate message based on game state\n\nStructure Layout (Game Unit data at offset 0x1b8/0x1c8):\nOffset   Size   Field           Type         Description\n0x1b8    4      pUnitData       void*        Unit composite data pointer\n0x1c8    4      pNextUnit       Unit*        Next unit in list\n0x1b4    4      dwUnknownFlag   dword        Release condition flag\n\nNote: Assembly-only variables (iVar1, uVar2, extraout_var) are compiler\ntemporaries optimized away in decompiled view. Phantom variable pbNameBuffer\nexists only in decompiler. Local stack array auStack_900[256] and local_800[1024]\nare buffer allocations for file enumeration and path building.",
