      "name": "ProcessBnetShutdown",
      "signature": "void ProcessBnetShutdown(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Handles Battle.net shutdown sequence and message loop termination.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call system initialization/setup (Ordinal_10003)\n2. Perform internal check via func_0x6fa85116\n3. If internal check succeeds AND login state is 0, return early\n4. Call Ordinal_10002 for additional cleanup\n5. If Ordinal_10002 succeeds and login state is still 0, return early\n6. Disable message processing (Ordinal_10028 with 0 parameter)\n7. Stop the main message loop (StopMessageLoop)\n8. Return 1\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\n1 on successful shutdown completion\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit at step 3 skips final message loop teardown\n- Early exit at step 5 skips Ordinal_10028 and StopMessageLoop\n- Login state (g_dwBnetLoginState) controls shutdown path\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0: Login state value indicating inactive connection\n- 1: Success return code",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:9fd4d7e908984943a88896efb97e5de0",
