      "name": "HandleBnetLoginCompletion",
      "signature": "uint HandleBnetLoginCompletion(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Handles Bnet login completion sequence.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10003() - Initialize/check Bnet connection state\n2. Call Ordinal_10031() and check return value\n3. If return is 0, call Ordinal_10002() to check additional state\n4. Check if g_dwBnetLoginState equals 0 (initial state)\n5. If login state confirmed, return 1 (success)\n6. Call Ordinal_10030(0) - Cleanup/finalize Bnet state\n7. Call StopMessageLoop() - Exit main message loop\n8. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nNone - No parameters required\n\nReturns:\nuint - 1 (success code)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return if login state is not initial (0)\n- Ordinal calls likely refer to D2Common.dll exports\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0: Initial/uninitialized state value\n- 1: Success return code",
