      "name": "HandleMessageLoopShutdown",
      "signature": "dword HandleMessageLoopShutdown(void)",
      "calling_convention": "unknown",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Callback handler invoked repeatedly by the message loop pump.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10003() to process current message state\n2. Call Ordinal_10061() to check if message processing is pending\n3. If result is 0 (no pending), call Ordinal_10002() to check connection status\n4. If connected (Ordinal_10002 != 0) AND login state is 0, signal success and exit (return 1)\n5. Otherwise, call Ordinal_10060(0) to reset state\n6. Call StopMessageLoop() to terminate the message pump\n7. Return 1 to indicate callback handled the message\n\nParameters:\nNone (callback handler with no parameters)\n\nReturns:\ndword: Always returns 1, indicating message was handled\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit at step 4 occurs only when specific connection conditions are met\n- The function controls both normal shutdown (Ordinal_10060) and early termination\n- Used as a callback parameter to MessagePumpLoop() in FUN_6fa808b0\n\nNote: Several Ordinal calls appear to be Fog.dll or Storm.dll functions\nrequiring ordinal mapping documentation for full clarity.",
