      "name": "CreateSubControl",
      "signature": "void * CreateSubControl(int nControlIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates and registers a new sub-control in the UI control factory pool.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that control pool has not exceeded MAX_CONTROLS (0x40 = 64)\n2. If exceeded, invoke FogAssert with location info (file, line 0x5f6)\n3. If assertion fails, exit with fatal error code (-1)\n4. Calculate control type descriptor offset: (nControlIndex * 0x30)\n5. Call CreateObjectByTypeFactory with pointer to descriptor\n6. Store returned Control pointer at g_pSubControlArray[g_dwNumSubControls]\n7. Increment g_dwNumSubControls counter\n8. Return new Control pointer to caller\n\nParameters:\n  nControlIndex (int, ECX register): Index into control type descriptor table\n                                     Used to calculate offset into g_pSubControlConfigTable\n                                     (stride = 0x30 = 48 bytes per descriptor)\n\nReturns:\n  void*: Pointer to newly created and registered Control object\n         NULL on fatal assertion failure (triggers process exit)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - MAX_CONTROLS boundary: 0x40 = 64 maximum controls allowed\n  - Assertion violation: Logs to source file location DIABLO2_SOURCE\\D2Lau at line 1526 (0x5f6)\n  - Pool management: Uses global counters and arrays to track allocations\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x40 (64):  MAX_CONTROLS limit for pool\n  0x30 (48):  Stride for control descriptor records in config table\n  0x5f6 (1526): Source file line number for assertion\n\nGlobal References:\n  g_dwNumSubControls (6fa97c5c):     Current count of allocated controls [0..64)\n  g_pSubControlConfigTable (6fa8f6b0): Pointer to control type descriptor table\n  g_pSubControlArray (6fa977a4):     Array of Control pointers (pool storage)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
