      "name": "CleanupAndReinitializeGameState",
      "signature": "void CleanupAndReinitializeGameState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Cleanup and reinitialize game state for new games or scene transitions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load UI object count and iterate through g_pUIObjectArray\n2. Dispatch each pending UI object handler via DispatchInventoryItemHandler\n3. Load pending control handler count from g_nPendingControlHandlerCount\n4. Iterate through g_aPendingControlHandlers and dispatch each via DispatchInventoryItemHandler\n5. Reset all handler counts to 0 (g_dwUIObjectCount, g_nPendingControlHandlerCount)\n6. Set baseline configuration via SetGlobalConfig(0)\n7. Check DAT_6fa97c84 flag to determine if palette reinitialization needed\n8. If flag set: build palette paths via wsprintfA using format \"%s\\%s\" with DATA_GLOBAL prefix\n9. Compare two palette buffers byte-by-byte for equality using ANSI string comparison\n10. Store comparison result as boolean (1=equal, 0=different) in g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x5a]\n11. Initialize palette with constructed paths via InitActPalette()\n12. Clear palette reinit flag DAT_6fa97c84 back to 0\n13. Release all game units and game object resources via ReleaseAllUnits()\n14. Clear unit hash table and cleanup structures via ClearHashTableAndCleanup()\n15. Mark state as cleaned via SetStoredValue(1)\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Palette reinitialization is conditionally triggered by DAT_6fa97c84 flag\n- Uses 2x260-byte stack buffers for constructing palette file paths\n- Palette comparison uses 2-byte stride for ANSI string comparison\n- No error handling; assumes all subsystem cleanup succeeds\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n- g_pUIObjectArray, g_dwUIObjectCount (UI object list cleared)\n- g_aPendingControlHandlers, g_nPendingControlHandlerCount (handlers cleared)\n- g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x5a] = palette equality flag\n- DAT_6fa97c84 (palette reinit flag, set to 1 then 0)\n- Unit tracking and hash table state (all units released)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:e81870a111965dd9737b816870441132",
