      "name": "SetBnetLoginStateReady",
      "signature": "void SetBnetLoginStateReady(void)",
      "calling_convention": "unknown",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets the Bnet login state to 1 (READY).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Write constant value 1 to global login state variable\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\n(void)\n\nPurpose:\nInitializes or updates the Bnet login state to indicate the connection is ready for use. This is a simple setter that writes a fixed state value to the global Bnet login state tracker.\n\nGlobal Variables Modified:\n- g_dwBnetLoginState (0x6fa97c88): Set to 1 (READY state)\n\nCross-References:\n- Called by 10 functions for Bnet initialization/state management\n- Read by GetBnetLoginState (0x6fa77540) to query current login state",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
