      "name": "CleanupBnetConnection",
      "signature": "void CleanupBnetConnection(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes pending control handler queue and clears the handler count.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load handler count from g_nPendingControlHandlerCount\n2. If count is zero or negative, skip to step 5\n3. Initialize loop counter (nIndex) to zero\n4. For each pending handler in g_aPendingControlHandlers array:\n   - Dispatch the handler via DispatchInventoryItemHandler\n   - Increment loop counter and advance handler pointer\n   - Compare counter against total count\n   - Repeat while counter < count\n5. Set g_nPendingControlHandlerCount to zero\n6. Return\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_nPendingControlHandlerCount <= 0, skips handler dispatch loop and zeroes count\n- Array access assumes g_aPendingControlHandlers is valid (non-null)\n\nCalled From:\n- ConnectToBattleNet (on network connection state changes)\n- PerformBnetLogin (on login completion)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6fa97c5c: Address of g_nPendingControlHandlerCount global\n- 0x6fa977a4: Address of g_aPendingControlHandlers array\n- 0x4: Size of each handler element (dword)\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error handling; relies on DispatchInventoryItemHandler to validate handlers",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:a116bb083f0d4f916b675518b660c2ca",
