      "name": "InitializeDisplayFromNetworkCheck",
      "signature": "int InitializeDisplayFromNetworkCheck(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes display state based on network address verification.\n\nCompares the local machine's IP address against a hardcoded expected address.\nIf the addresses match (local host), converts the IP string to Unicode and enables\ntwo display control handlers. If the addresses don't match (remote connection),\ndisplays an error message and disables those handlers.\n\nALGORITHM:\n1. Retrieve local machine IP address via GetLocalIPAddress()\n2. Clear the display text object\n3. Perform byte-by-byte string comparison of IP address with g_szLocalHostIPAddress\n   - Compare using wide character (2-byte) stride for case-insensitive comparison\n   - Loop until null terminator (byte 0x00) encountered\n4. If comparison result indicates match (iVar3 != 0):\n   a. Convert IP address string to Unicode format\n   b. Enable UI control handler 0x43 (primary display)\n   c. Enable UI control handler 0x51 (secondary display)\n5. Else (IP addresses don't match):\n   a. Retrieve error message string ID 0x1404\n   b. Add formatted error text to display object\n   c. Disable UI control handler 0x43\n   d. Disable UI control handler 0x51\n6. Set UI control handler 0x50 (status indicator) to match comparison result\n7. Return success status (1)\n\nPARAMETERS:\n(none - __stdcall)\n\nRETURNS:\nEAX = 1 (always returns success)\n\nVARIABLES:\nlpsz_RemoteIP: IP address string returned from GetLocalIPAddress()\npb_CurrentRemoteChar: Pointer walking through remote IP string (2-byte increments)\npb_CompareChar: Pointer walking through comparison string (2-byte increments)\nby_CurrentByte: Current byte being compared\nf_IsRemoteLess: Boolean result of less-than comparison (for SBB logic)\nn_CompareResult: Final string comparison result (-1, 0, or 1)\nwsz_ErrorMessage: Error message string pointer (unused in decompiled flow - assembly artifact)\n\nSPECIAL CASES:\n- String comparison uses 2-byte stride to compare full characters at once\n- The SBB instruction pattern (at 0x6fa786a4) implements signed comparison logic\n  for the final result: (1 - bfVar5) - (uint)(bfVar5 != 0) produces -1, 0, or 1\n- Control handler indices (0x43, 0x51, 0x50) are accessed via array subscript from base at 0x6fa978xx\n\nERROR HANDLING:\n- No error conditions detected; function always returns 1\n- If GetLocalIPAddress() fails, comparison against empty string occurs\n- If display object is NULL, subsequent calls may fail gracefully\n\nCROSS-REFERENCES:\nCalled by: (none found - likely initialization routine called via vtable or direct call)\nCalls: GetLocalIPAddress, ClearTextDataList, ConvertStringToUnicode, ValidateStringId,\n       TextBoxAddTextWithDefaults, SetUnitBitMask\n\nGLOBALS USED:\ng_pDisplayTextObject (0x6fa97640): Display text object pointer\ng_szLocalHostIPAddress (0x6fa92b68): Expected local IP address string\ng_aPendingControlHandlers[0x43]: Primary UI control handler (display state)\ng_aPendingControlHandlers[0x51]: Secondary UI control handler (display state)\ng_aPendingControlHandlers[0x50]: Status indicator handler",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
