      "name": "InitializeGameUIAndRecreateObjects",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameUIAndRecreateObjects(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Reinitialize game UI and recreate all UI objects during disconnection/state reset\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set _g_dwBnetConnectionActive flag and call DisconnectFromBnet()\n2. Iterate UI objects in g_pUIObjectArray (count g_dwUIObjectCount) - dispatch each via DispatchInventoryItemHandler()\n3. Clear UI state: reset pending handler count (g_nPendingControlHandlerCount), clear unknown flags, zero UI object count\n4. Iterate pending handlers in g_aPendingControlHandlers (count g_nPendingControlHandlerCount) - dispatch each\n5. Call SetGlobalConfig(0) to reset configuration\n6. If g_bPaletteReinitFlag set: call InitializePaletteFromPath with fechar palette paths\n7. Call ReleaseAllUnits() to free unit objects and ClearHashTableAndCleanup() to reset hash tables\n8. Call SetStoredValue(1) to store state\n9. Build formatted path strings for sky and fechar palettes using wsprintfA()\n10. Byte-by-byte comparison of sky vs fechar palette files (2-byte stride loop until null terminator)\n11. Store comparison result (equal=1, not equal=-1) in g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x5a]\n12. Initialize Act Palette via InitActPalette() with formatted paths\n13. Create UI objects in sequence, checking max count 0x40 before each (assert/fatal error if exceeded):\n    - DAT_6fa925c0 object, add text string id 0x13fd via TextBoxAddTextWithDefaults()\n    - DAT_6fa925f0 object, add to array\n    - DAT_6fa92620 object, store at handler[0x50], add text id 0x1401\n    - DAT_6fa92680 object, store at handler[0x43]\n    - DAT_6fa926b0 object, store at handler[0x51]\n    - DAT_6fa926e0 object, store at handler[0x56], add text id 0x1402\n    - DAT_6fa92710 object, store at handler[0x57], add text id 0x1403\n14. Clear bit masks for handler[0x56] and handler[0x57] objects via SetOrClearBitMask(obj, 0)\n15. Create DAT_6fa92740 button object and set as current input via SetCurrentInputItem()\n16. Create DAT_6fa92770 timer object, store in DAT_6fa97674 and handler[0], reset via ResetTimerData()\n17. Set timer context handler via SetTimerContextHandler(pTimer)\n18. Create DAT_6fa92650 display text object, store in g_pDisplayTextObject\n19. Call FUN_6fa78be0() to configure UI render/display settings\n20. Return to caller\n\nParameters: none (void __stdcall)\n\nReturns: void (no return value, performs initialization side effects)",
