      "comment": "Initializes and displays the realm character error dialog UI after Battle.net login failure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call HandleRealmCharacterError() to construct and display the error dialog UI\n2. Return success code (1) to caller\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: dword - Returns 1 (success/continue code)\n\nDescription:\nThin wrapper function providing standardized entry point for displaying the Battle.net character\nlogin error dialog. The wrapped function HandleRealmCharacterError() performs all substantial work\nincluding UI creation (~10 objects), population of error messages and instructions from the string\ntable, setup of character name/password input fields, and configuration of tab navigation controls.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- Return value 1: Success indicator",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f9a61880c017be62a40eb11ac6850881",
