      "name": "HandleControlStateTransition",
      "signature": "int HandleControlStateTransition(void * pControlHandler, dword dwCoordinates)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Processes control state transitions based on game state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x59] for current state code (0, 1, 2, or 3)\n2. For state 3: Clear pending state, reset control panel, set state to 3\n3. For state 0: Process input coordinates, initialize control state\n4. For state 2: Process default state, initialize control state\n5. For state 1: Call FUN_6fa81f10 for special handling\n6. Call StopMessageLoop() after state processing\n7. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pControlHandler (void* in ECX): Implicit __fastcall parameter (unused in decompilation)\n  dwCoordinates (dword in EDX): Packed coordinate value (Y in high word, used for mouseover)\n\nReturns:\n  int: 1 (success)\n\nState Codes:\n  0: Initialize mode with input coordinates\n  1: Special handler mode (calls FUN_6fa81f10)\n  2: Reset mode\n  3: Cleanup mode\n\nKey Offsets into Handler Structure (g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x53]):\n  0x14: Reset field\n  0x53: Handler pointer index\n  0x58: State flag\n  0x59: State code\n  0xb8: Control panel data\n  0xd0: Control flag\n  0xe8: Control offset\n  0x1e9: Mode flags\n  0x1ea: Mode flags (extended)\n  0x204: Control state flags\n  0x225: Control reset flag\n  0x356: Control type",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:546c17e22a38a8e15c8829671ea3e893",
