      "name": "ValidateCdKeyInputFields",
      "signature": "void ValidateCdKeyInputFields(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Validates CD key input edit box fields and updates UI dialog validation state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve text pointer from first edit box (control handler index 0x4e)\n2. Retrieve text pointer from second edit box (control handler index 0x44)\n3. Initialize validation flag to 0 (invalid) via XOR EBP,EBP\n4. If both edit boxes contain text:\n   a. Calculate length of first edit box text via strlen call\n   b. Calculate length of second edit box text via strlen call\n   c. Validate bounds: first must be 1-16 (0x1-0x10), second must be 1-13 (0x1-0xd)\n   d. If all bounds valid, set validation flag to 1 (valid)\n5. If current UI dialog object exists (g_pCurrentUIDialogObject != NULL)\n   Call SetUnitBitMask(pDialog, nValidationMask)\n6. Return via pop EBX, EBP, ESI; RET\n\nParameters:\nNone - Uses global state:\n  g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x4e] - First edit box control handle\n  g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x44] - Second edit box control handle\n  g_pCurrentUIDialogObject - Current dialog for mask update\n\nReturns:\nNone - Updates UI state via SetUnitBitMask\n\nRegister Usage (Assembly Mapping):\n- EBP: nValidationMask (0 or 1 flag)\n- ESI: nKeyLength (strlen result)\n- EBX: nValueLength (strlen result)\n- EDI: strlen function pointer (0x6fa8d040)\n- ECX: Parameter register for function calls\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If either edit box is NULL, validation fails (flag stays 0)\n- If nKeyLength < 1 or > 16, validation fails\n- If nValueLength < 1 or > 13, validation fails\n- If g_pCurrentUIDialogObject is NULL, SetUnitBitMask is not called\n\nCalled By: HandleCdKeyErrorReconnect (at 0x6fa78110)\nDepends On: strlen (C runtime), D2Win_GetEditBoxChild, SetUnitBitMask",
