      "name": "ReleaseShardArrayAllocations",
      "signature": "int ReleaseShardArrayAllocations(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Releases all allocated memory pools for the global shard array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global shard array pointer (g_pShardArray) is non-null\n2. If null, return 1 (success)\n3. If non-null, iterate through each shard in the array:\n   - Load shard pointer from g_pShardArray[i]\n   - Validate shard pointer is non-null\n   - Check field at offset 0x20 (allocation marker):\n     * If 0: Assert failure (code should not reach here)\n     * If non-0: Call ReleasePoolAllocation for allocated sub-pools\n   - Check field at offset 0x1c (additional data):\n     * If non-0: Call ReleasePoolAllocation twice more\n4. After loop, call ReleasePoolAllocation one final time\n5. Set g_pShardArray to NULL\n6. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  (none) - Function operates on global state\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 on success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_pShardArray is NULL, immediately returns 1\n  - Assertion failures trigger FatalErrorExit(-1)\n  - Function is called during game cleanup and player data loading\n\nNote: Decompilation contains unreachable code paths due to control flow complexity.\nThe actual execution path is straightforward loop with exception handlers.",
