      "comment": "Initialize and configure all inventory control UI elements and game object arrays.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Release previously allocated game objects from object pool\n2. Reset game object counter and allocation flags\n3. Create or load primary inventory object via CreateObjectByTypeFactory\n4. Validate inventory count does not exceed 64 maximum\n5. Create secondary inventory object if first load\n6. Initialize inventory UI controls (title, description, main display)\n7. Set unit flags for inventory controls via SetUnitFlags\n8. Load string table entry 0x147B for inventory display text\n9. Apply text to control via TextBoxAddTextWithDefaults\n10. Setup UI message pump to process events\n11. Initialize game session data with game state pointer\n12. Build complete inventory item array from game data\n13. Allocate and populate inventory item structures for each item\n14. Dispatch inventory handlers for each created item control\n15. Store inventory count in global for runtime access\n\nParameters: void (no parameters)\n\nReturns: void (always succeeds, calls FatalErrorExit on critical failures)",
