      "name": "IsFeatureEnabled",
      "signature": "int IsFeatureEnabled(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Checks if a feature is enabled.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return constant 1 (TRUE)\n\nParameters:\n  (none)\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (feature enabled/TRUE)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  This is a stub function that unconditionally returns TRUE. It may represent:\n  - A feature flag that is always enabled\n  - A placeholder for future conditional logic\n  - A validation function that always succeeds\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x1 - Constant return value (TRUE)\n\nNote:\n  The function appears in a function pointer table at 0x6fa7be6a,\n  indicating it's likely part of a dispatch table or feature check system.",
