      "name": "LoadFrontEndUIImages",
      "signature": "void LoadFrontEndUIImages(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Loads all front-end UI control images and stores handles in global array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 260-byte buffer (MAX_PATH) on stack for image path construction\n2. Initialize ESI with pointer to wsprintfA function from import table\n3. For each UI image element:\n   a. Call wsprintfA to format image path with data directory prefix\n   b. Call LoadCelImage to load image from file\n   c. Store returned image handle in g_aPendingControlHandlers array\n4. Conditionally load expansion-specific (LoD) UI variants:\n   a. Call CheckExpansionMpqExists to test for Lord of Destruction MPQ\n   b. If present, load 4 additional expansion-only UI screens\n   c. Otherwise use base game UI variants\n\nParameters:\n(none - function uses global state only)\nIMPLICIT g_aPendingControlHandlers (uint array for image handles)\nIMPLICIT s_DATA_GLOBAL (global data directory path string)\nIMPLICIT g_aGameResourceDirectory (resource directory configuration)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (all UI images loaded into g_aPendingControlHandlers array at specific indices)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Expansion detection affects images at indices: 0xa4, 0xa6, 0xa9-0xab, 0xba, 0xc0-0xc1, 0xd0\n- Base game uses variant strings from data: trademark, title screen, realm select, TCP/IP\n- Expansion appends \"Ex\" suffix or alternate file names for LoD-specific assets\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x104 - Stack buffer size (260 bytes = MAX_PATH)\n0x9c-0xd3 - Control handler array indices for specific UI elements\n0x6fa8d40c - Pointer to wsprintfA function import\n0x6fa97a14 - Base address of g_aPendingControlHandlers array (26 elements minimum)\n\nError Handling:\nNo error checking. Assumes all LoadCelImage calls succeed and return valid handles.\nNo validation of returned image handles or file existence checks.",
