      "comment": "Algorithm:\n1. Clear existing UI object array by calling DispatchInventoryItemHandler for each\n2. Reset UI object count and internal control handler arrays\n3. Clear pending control handlers\n4. Reset game object count\n5. Call SetGlobalConfig(0) to clear stored configurations\n6. If palette reinit flag set, reinitialize palette from fechar data files\n7. Release all active game units from memory\n8. Clear hash table and cleanup resources\n9. Create 5 UI objects via CreateObjectByTypeFactory with bounds checking (max 0x40 objects):\n   - Object 1: DAT_6fa8f710\n   - Object 2: DAT_6fa8f740\n   - Object 3: DAT_6fa8f7d0\n   - Object 4: DAT_6fa8f800\n   - Object 5: DAT_6fa8f770\n10. After object 4, set palette reinit flag to trigger palette initialization\n11. Initialize sky palette from fechar_pal files\n12. Compare fechar_pal.dat against sky_pal.dat paths, store result in g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x5a]\n13. Call InitActPalette to apply palette changes\n14. Check for expansion MPQ and set text string IDs accordingly (0x557a for expansion, 0x13f0/0x13f1 for base)\n15. Add text strings to UI object 5\n16. Reset music configuration\n17. Initialize music tracks if music options enabled\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Bounds checking before each UI object add with FogAssert on overflow\n- Palette comparison handles multi-byte string matching\n- Expansion MPQ check affects which text strings are used\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x40: Maximum UI object count (64 decimal)\n- 0x3f: Maximum index check (63 = 0x40 - 1)\n- 0x5a: UI object array index for palette comparison flag (90 decimal)\n- 0x557a, 0x13f0, 0x13f1: String IDs for game state messages\n- 0x208: Stack allocation size (520 decimal)\n\nError Handling:\n- FogAssert called on UI object array overflow before FatalErrorExit(-1)\n- All callees return without explicit error checking\n\nMemory Layout:\ng_pUIObjectArray: Global array of UI object pointers\ng_dwUIObjectCount: Current UI object count in array\ng_aPendingControlHandlers: Array for game object handlers and state storage\ng_dwGameObjectCount: Current game object count\ng_bPaletteReinitFlag: Flag to trigger palette reinitialization\n\nStructure Notes:\nUses DAT_6fa8f* references which are UI object type factory descriptors\nAccesses palette data through PTR_s_palette_* string references",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
