      "name": "InitiateCdKeyErrorHandler",
      "signature": "void InitiateCdKeyErrorHandler(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize CD Key authentication error recovery handler and flag pending control operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set global flag g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x59] to 1 to mark pending control handler state\n2. Call HandleCdKeyErrorReconnect() to initialize BNet reconnection UI\n3. Return success (1)\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns:\n  1 (success) - Handler initialized and pending UI setup initiated\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Flag is set in global control handler array at fixed index 0x59\n  - Actual UI initialization delegated to HandleCdKeyErrorReconnect()\n  - No parameters, minimal logic - pure state flag setter\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  - 0x59: Array index for CD key error control handler flag\n  - 0x6fa97908: Address of g_aPendingControlHandlers global array\n\nError Handling:\n  - No error handling; always succeeds\n  - Assumes HandleCdKeyErrorReconnect() validates state\n\nMemory Model:\n  - Global state management: g_aPendingControlHandlers array tracks pending UI operations\n  - No local variables or stack usage beyond minimal register allocation\n  - Single write to global array element, then tail-call semantics to handler\n\nCalled by: Unknown (no xrefs found - likely data pointer or callback table reference)\nCalls: HandleCdKeyErrorReconnect (BNet auth error UI initialization)",
