      "name": "ValidateMouseClickInput",
      "signature": "bool ValidateMouseClickInput(void * pInputEvent)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Validates mouse input events for single-click detection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract message code from input event (pInputEvent + 0x4)\n2. Get current system tick count via GetTickCount()\n3. Calculate time delta from last recorded tick\n4. Get current cursor position via GetCursorPos()\n5. Calculate absolute X and Y position deltas from last position\n6. Calculate Manhattan distance (|deltaX| + |deltaY|) from last position\n7. Validate: message code must be 0x201 (WM_LBUTTONDOWN)\n8. Validate: time delta must be <= 300ms (0x12c)\n9. Validate: position delta must be <= 4 pixels (click threshold)\n10. Return true if all validations pass (single valid click), false otherwise\n11. Update global tracking variables with current tick and cursor position\n\nParameters:\n  pInputEvent (ECX IMPLICIT): void* - Pointer to input event structure\n    Offset +0x4: uint dwMessageCode - Windows message code\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: bool - true if input is valid single-click, false otherwise\n\nGlobal Data Modified:\n  DAT_6fa97ca0: uint - Last recorded system tick count\n  DAT_6fa97ca8: uint - Last recorded cursor X position\n  DAT_6fa97cac: uint - Last recorded cursor Y position\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x201: WM_LBUTTONDOWN message code\n  0x12c (300 decimal): Maximum milliseconds between clicks (debounce window)\n  0x4: Pixel threshold for click position stability\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - First call initializes global tracking variables to current values\n  - Manhattan distance metric prevents diagonal movements beyond threshold\n  - Time check prevents click detection outside debounce window\n  - Message code validation ensures only left button down events processed",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
