      "name": "InitializeGameUIObjectsAndPalette",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameUIObjectsAndPalette(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "InitializeGameUIObjectsAndPalette - Initialize UI controls and palette configuration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x208 bytes (260*2) stack frame for file path buffers\n2. Compare palette source files (sky .pl2 vs .dat) byte-by-byte\n   - Load source pointers from global data table\n   - Format file paths with data directory prefix\n   - Compare using word-aligned reads in loop\n3. Store comparison result in control handler at index 0x5a\n4. Initialize palette actor from formatted path strings\n5. Dispatch inventory item handler to update UI state\n6. Validate object count (must be <= 0x3f)\n7. Create UI objects from factory in sequence:\n   - Create object from DAT_6fa92830, store in handler array[0]\n   - Create object from DAT_6fa92800, store in handler array[1]\n   - Create object from DAT_6fa927a0, initialize with string 0x2a54\n   - Create edit control from DAT_6fa927d0, set as current input\n   - Create object from DAT_6fa92860, set as current item\n   - Create object from DAT_6fa92890, store in handler array[5]\n8. Increment global object counter after each creation\n9. Initialize screenshot config from edit control\n\nParameters:\nNone (void)\n\nReturns:\nEAX = 1 (always returns success)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:1de091de38a0c8104999bec46fd52d0f",
