      "name": "ProcessBattleNetLogin",
      "signature": "dword ProcessBattleNetLogin(char * lpszCharacterName, ushort wOptions, char bAccountInfo, byte * pbAccountData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "ProcessBattleNetLogin - Authenticate character to Battle.Net and initialize game session\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy character name (lpszCharacterName) to global control handler buffer at offset 0xB8\n2. Copy account data (pbAccountData) to global control handler buffer at offset 0xD0\n3. Store account flags (wOptions) at handler offset 0x1EA\n4. Call FUN_6fa81710 to prepare login handler\n5. Check global login state (g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x59]):\n   - If state 1 or 3: Query pBnclientInterface->unkOffset74() for connection status\n     - If not connected: Call FUN_6fa85070, ConnectToBattleNet, PerformBnetLogin\n     - Return 0 on connection failure\n   - If state 0: Initialize single-player mode (character 0x356=1, flags 0x204=0x4/0x804)\n   - If state 2: Initialize other game mode (character 0x356=3)\n   - Otherwise: Process account data via FUN_6fa83a50\n6. If account verification fails: Display error messages (0x145B/0x145C)\n7. If account expired (input 2): Create character selection dialog with expired notice\n8. Create game UI controls and message pump loop for login completion handler\n9. Return 1 on success, 0 on failure\n\nParameters:\n  lpszCharacterName (ECX): ANSI null-terminated character name string\n  wOptions (DX): Login option flags (bit 2=0x4 for specific mode, bit 5=0x20 for special)\n  bAccountInfo (Stack[0x4]): Account info flag byte\n  pbAccountData (Stack[0x8]): Pointer to account data structure\n\nReturns:\n  EAX=1 on successful login/initialization, EAX=0 on failure (connection failed, login failed, etc.)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x5A]: Determines which UI config set to load (ConfigTypeA vs ConfigTypeB)\n- Character state 0x356 can be: 1=online, 2=offline, 3=alternate, 4=custom\n- Handler offset 0x204 stores mode flags (base 0x4, or 0x804 if option 0x4 set, or 0x100004 if special mode)\n- Character 0x1EA stores option flags via MOVZX from input parameter wOptions\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x53: Global control handler index for character selection\n  0x58: Global login control flow state (1=ready, 3=cleanup)\n  0x59: Global game mode indicator (0=single, 1=battle.net, 2=ladder, 3=other)\n  0x5A: Config variant selector (0=ConfigA, 1=ConfigB)\n  0xB8: Offset for character name buffer in handler (256 byte Unicode buffer at +0x100)\n  0xD0: Offset for account data in handler (256 byte Unicode buffer)\n  0x14: Handler initialization flag field\n  0x1EA: Login option flags field (word)\n  0x204: Game mode flags field (dword)\n  0x225: Custom state field (byte)\n  0x356: Character state field (byte)\n  0x46, 0x7B, 0x2, 0x47, 0x145B, 0x145C, 0x147B, 0x140D, 0x275A: String IDs for UI messages\n  0xD7-0xDA, 0xD9, 0xF0-0xF3, 0xF2: Control type IDs for UI construction\n\nControl Message Flow:\n  - Returns 0 immediately if BattleNet connection fails\n  - Returns 0 if PerformBnetLogin fails\n  - Returns 1 if single-player mode initialized\n  - Returns 1 if ladder/alternate mode initialized with option 0x20 (special mode flag)\n  - Enters message pump (MessagePumpLoop) for interactive login\n  - Calls SetBnetLoginStateReady/RequestGameShutdown/ResetGameStateAndCleanup as handlers\n  \nStack Layout:\n  [ESP+0x4]: Return address (caller responsibility)\n  [ESP+0x8]: pbAccountData parameter (byte pointer)\n  [ESP+0xC]: bAccountInfo parameter (char)\n  [ESP+0x10]: Copy of bAccountInfo (stack copy for local use)\n  [ESP+0x14-0x113]: aUStack_100 - Unicode buffer (256 chars = 0x100 bytes)\n  [ESP+0x114-0x213]: aUStack_200 - Unicode buffer (256 chars = 0x100 bytes)\n  [ESP-0x204]: Local frame base\n\nHidden Variables (Assembly-Only):\n  local_204 (Stack[-0x204]): Frame size marker, not used in decompiled code",
