      "name": "ValidateBNetLoginCredentials",
      "signature": "int ValidateBNetLoginCredentials(int nInitializationFlag)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Validates BNet login credentials and initializes game state upon successful authentication.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Check if parameter is zero; return error if true\\n2. Extract username, password, and account from edit box controls\\n3. Convert Unicode strings to Windows ANSI encoding (256 byte buffers)\\n4. Validate username: minimum 2 chars, maximum 16 chars\\n5. Validate password: minimum 2 chars, maximum 21 chars\\n6. Validate password confirmation matches password field\\n7. Clear state flag g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x9b]\\n8. Call PerformBnetLogin with account and flags\\n9. If login succeeds, store account name to registry and reinitialize game state\\n10. Return 1 on success or error (0 on cancelled validation)\\n\\nParameters:\\n  nInitializationFlag - Initialization/state parameter (0 triggers error handler)\\n\\nReturns:\\n  int - 1 = success or error handled, continues; 0 = operation cancelled\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  Handles CD key errors, palette reinitialization, UI object cleanup\\n  \\nMagic Numbers: Control indices 0x4e/0x44/0x4d, field offsets 0x53/0x88/0xa0,\\nerror codes 0x1460-0x1464, string buffer 0x100 bytes",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
