      "name": "WaitForGameResourceReady",
      "signature": "uint WaitForGameResourceReady(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Waits for a game resource to become ready with synchronization support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if resource already initialized via global flag g_fGameResourceInitialized\n2. If initialized, return success code 1 immediately\n3. Acquire resource handle by calling Ordinal_10055\n4. If acquisition fails (returns 0), return error code 2\n5. Wait for resource with infinite timeout (0)\n6. Interpret wait result: 0=ready, 0x102=timeout, other=error\n7. Return appropriate status code\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nuint: Status code\n  0 - Resource is ready (WaitForSingleObject succeeded)\n  1 - Resource already initialized (cached state)\n  2 - Resource acquisition or wait failed\n  3 - Resource wait timed out (WAIT_TIMEOUT = 0x102)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThe function performs a non-blocking check via the global flag before attempting\nto acquire and wait on the actual resource. Ordinal_10055 appears to be a resource\nfactory or getter function specific to the game engine.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x102 - WAIT_TIMEOUT Windows constant, indicates timeout occurred\n0 - WAIT_OBJECT_0 Windows constant, indicates object was signaled",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
