      "comment": "Process all pending inventory item handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global count of pending handlers (g_dwGameObjectCount)\n2. If count is 0, reset count and return 1 (success)\n3. Otherwise, iterate through handler array (g_aPendingControlHandlers)\n4. Call DispatchInventoryItemHandler for each handler with pointer to handler value\n5. Increment loop counter after each handler processed\n6. After all handlers processed, clear count and return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  void\n\nReturns:\n  int: Always returns 1 (success status)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If no handlers pending (g_dwGameObjectCount == 0), function returns immediately after resetting counter\n  - Handler array pointer arithmetic: pdwHandler incremented by 1 (sizeof uint = 4 bytes)\n\nGlobal State:\n  g_dwGameObjectCount: Counter of pending handlers to process (reset to 0 after processing)\n  g_aPendingControlHandlers: Array of handler values to dispatch (uint[256])\n\nError Handling:\n  Function always returns 1 regardless of handler processing results\n  Errors from DispatchInventoryItemHandler are ignored/swallowed",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:546c17e22a38a8e15c8829671ea3e893",
