      "name": "InitializeInventoryControlPanel",
      "signature": "void InitializeInventoryControlPanel(Unicode * pszInventoryText, int nPanelConfig)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize Inventory Control Panel with multi-line text content.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dispatch all pending control event handlers (g_dwGameObjectCount items)\n2. Reset handler count to zero\n3. Create base panel control object via factory (g_pConfigTypeA)\n4. Push to handler array and increment count\n5. Validate handler count <= 0x40 (max 64 handlers)\n6. Create sub-control object via factory with computed type offset\n7. Push to handler array and increment count\n8. Create text box control object via factory (g_pConfigTypeA_Sub)\n9. Push to handler array and increment count\n10. Set unit flags on all three controls (panel, sub-control, textbox)\n11. Initialize 0x400-byte wide-char buffer using Unicode default constructor\n12. Copy input text to buffer via strncpy (max 0x400 wchars)\n13. Parse buffer for newline characters (L'\\\n')\n14. Split text by newlines and add each segment to textbox\n15. Add final segment if text extends to end\n\nParameters:\n- ECX (param_1): Unicode * pszInventoryText - Source inventory display text (may contain \\\n)\n- EDX (param_2): int nPanelConfig - Configuration index (0/1 for type offset calculation)\n\nReturns:\n- void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handler array limit is 0x40 (64 maximum); excess triggers FatalErrorExit\n- Text buffer limited to 0x400 wide characters (~1KB)\n- Empty input (nul terminator at start) skips text parsing\n- Newline at end creates empty segment (skipped by extent check)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3f = 63 (max valid handler index, check at 0x3f < count)\n- 0x40 = 64 (max handler count threshold)\n- 0x800 = 2048 (stack allocation for local_800 - double buffer size)\n- 0x400 = 1024 (max wide character count in text buffer)\n- 0x5f6 = 1526 (assertion line number from source)\n\nError Handling:\n- FogAssert called if handler count exceeds 0x3f (assertion 0x5f6)\n- FatalErrorExit(-1) called on assertion failure\n- No validation of input pointer pszInventoryText (assumed valid)\n\nControl Flow:\n- Initial handler dispatch loop (lines 0x6fa847e0-0x6fa84801)\n- Text parsing loop processes wchar_t stream (lines 0x6fa84913-0x6fa84943)\n- Buffer initialization loop via constructor (lines 0x6fa848f4-0x6fa84900)\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n- g_dwGameObjectCount: Reset to 0, then incremented 3 times\n- g_aPendingControlHandlers: Array populated with 3 control objects\n- _g_pBnetDisconnectHandler: Loaded from EDX (unaff_EBX), written at func exit\n- g_pConfigTypeA, g_pConfigTypeA_Sub: Used as factory type parameters",
