      "name": "SetGameStateFlag",
      "signature": "void SetGameStateFlag(int nEnabled)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets game state flag bit 1 if the specified condition is true.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nEnabled parameter is non-zero (TEST ECX, ECX)\n2. If zero, skip to RET (conditional jump)\n3. If non-zero, set bit 1 in g_dwGameStateFlags (OR dword with 0x2)\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- nEnabled (int): Condition flag. Non-zero value triggers bit set.\n\nReturns:\n- void (implicit in __fastcall via registers)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Bit 1 (mask 0x2) is set only when nEnabled != 0\n- If already set, operation is idempotent\n- Called during character creation and game state transitions\n\nGlobal Flags Layout (g_dwGameStateFlags):\n- Bit 0 (0x1): [Purpose unknown]\n- Bit 1 (0x2): Set by SetGameStateFlag when condition true\n- Bits 2-31: [Other state flags]\n\nCalling Convention: __fastcall\n- Parameter 1 (nEnabled) passed in ECX register\n- Return via RET instruction (void return)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:07c91129d1827ff4a9259e0f0d611786",
