      "name": "ProcessAndDeleteFiles",
      "signature": "void ProcessAndDeleteFiles(char * lpszSearchPattern, char * lpszSubdirectory)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Searches and deletes matching files in the save directory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate lpszSearchPattern is not empty, assert and exit if empty\n2. Get save directory path via GetSaveDirectoryPath into stack buffer\n3. If lpszSubdirectory provided: format directory path, create recursively, copy to buffer\n4. Format search pattern by combining prefix with lpszSearchPattern\n5. Call FindFirstFileA with pattern to begin file enumeration\n6. Enter main loop while file handle remains valid:\n   - Format target file path with g_szFilePrefix\n   - Call GetFileAttributesA to check file properties\n   - If FILE_ATTRIBUTE_DIRECTORY (0x10) is set: skip to FindNextFileA\n   - Otherwise: Call DeleteFileA to remove regular file\n   - If delete fails: return immediately\n   - Restart enumeration with FindFirstFileA on pattern\n7. Exit loop when handle becomes invalid (INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE)\n\nParameters:\n- lpszSearchPattern (ECX): Search pattern string (e.g., \"*.sav\")\n- lpszSubdirectory (EDX): Optional subdirectory name, NULL if not used\n\nReturns: void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty search pattern triggers assertion failure and fatal error exit\n- Directories are enumerated but never deleted\n- Each successful file deletion causes search restart\n- Failed deletion causes immediate function exit\n- Handle invalidation terminates enumeration\n\nGlobal References:\n- g_szFilePrefix: File path prefix constant used in formatting\n- Search pattern format strings in data section\n\nStack Frame:\n- [ESP+0x10]: Save directory path buffer (260 bytes)\n- [ESP+0x114]: WIN32_FIND_DATAA structure (320 bytes)\n- [ESP+0x254]: Search path string (504 bytes)\n- [ESP+0x358]: Target file path string (500 bytes)",
