      "name": "LoadAndProcessSaveFile",
      "signature": "uint LoadAndProcessSaveFile(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Loads and validates a Diablo II save file, extracting character data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 9716-byte buffer for file operations (0x25f4 = 0x2000 + headers)\n2. Get save directory path (/Save)\n3. Construct save file path with extension\n4. Open file with FUN_6fa85b4b (fopen wrapper)\n5. Read up to 0x2000 bytes using FUN_6fa85a03 (fread wrapper)\n6. Validate file size exceeds minimum (0x81 bytes)\n7. Verify save file magic marker (0xaa55aa55) at offset 0x00\n8. Check version byte at offset 0x04 (valid: 0x47-0x57 for patch versions)\n9. If valid, encode character data:\n   - 7-byte header encoding\n   - Character name/class from offset 0x26 (11 bytes) or alternate location\n   - Experience, level, and attribute data\n   - Resource counts (mana, health) with defaults\n   - 3-byte difficulty flags (0xff for unset)\n10. Close file with FUN_6fa85986 (fclose wrapper)\n11. Return 1 on success, 0 on failure\n\nParameters:\n(none - uses implicit __stdcall register parameters)\n\nReturns:\nEBX: Success flag (1=valid save processed, 0=error/invalid)\n\nStructure Layout (Save File Header):\nOffset | Size | Field              | Type     | Notes\n-------|------|-------------------|----------|------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | dwMagic           | uint     | 0xaa55aa55 magic marker\n0x04   | 1    | bVersion          | byte     | 0x47-0x57 patch versions\n0x05   | 1    | bExpansion        | byte     | Expansion flag\n0x06   | 4    | dwChecksum        | uint     | File checksum\n0x0a   | 1    | bDifficulty       | byte     | Difficulty setting\n0x0b   | 1    | bClassId          | byte     | Class ID\n0x0c   | 2    | wFlags            | ushort   | Character flags\n0x0e   | 11   | szCharName        | char[11] | Character name (null-term)\n0x19   | 4    | dwExperience      | uint     | Total experience\n0x1d   | 1    | bLevel            | byte     | Character level\n0x1e   | 4    | dwStatPoints      | uint     | Unallocated stat points\n0x22   | 1    | bHotkeys          | byte     | Hotkey selection\n0x23   | 4    | nMana             | int      | Mana points\n0x27   | 4    | nHealth           | int      | Hit points\n0x2b   | 2    | wManaMax          | ushort   | Maximum mana\n0x2d   | 1    | bHealthMax        | byte     | Maximum health offset\n... (character data continues)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x25f4: Stack buffer size (9716 bytes = 0x2000 file + headers)\n- 0x2000: Maximum file read size\n- 0x81: Minimum valid file size (129 bytes)\n- 0xaa55aa55: Save file magic marker\n- 0x47-0x57: Valid version bytes (patch versions D2:LoD 1.0x)\n- 0xff: Default value for unset difficulty flags\n\nError Handling:\n- If save path string is empty: FatalErrorExit(0xffffffff)\n- If file open fails: Return 0\n- If file size < 129 bytes: Return 0\n- If magic marker mismatch: Return 0\n- If version not in valid range: Return 0\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Character name location varies: standard at offset 0x1e (11 bytes) or\n  alternate layout used by some D2 versions\n- Difficulty flags default to 0xff if zero (uninitialized)\n- File handle closed by FUN_6fa85986 (error handling wrapper)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
