      "name": "UpdateGameSaveFlags",
      "signature": "int UpdateGameSaveFlags(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Updates game save file by setting a persistence flag.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get save game directory path\n2. Build path to save file (\"s_s_d2s\")\n3. Open save file with read-write access (0xc0000000 = GENERIC_READ|GENERIC_WRITE)\n4. If file open fails, return 0 (error)\n5. Read file header (0x82 bytes) from file start\n6. Seek to offset 0x18 in file\n7. OR flag value at offset 0x2c with 0x20 (set persistence bit)\n8. Write modified 4-byte flag value back to file at offset 0x18\n9. Close file handle\n10. Return success/failure status from write operation\n\nParameters:\n(none) - Uses static save directory path and hardcoded save filename\n\nReturns:\nSuccess: non-zero value from WriteFileWrapper (bytes written)\nFailure: 0 if file cannot be opened\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If CreateFileWrapper fails, returns immediately with 0\n- Flag is OR'd with 0x20 (sets bit 5 = persistence/completion flag)\n- File pointer is repositioned to 0x18 before writing\n- abFileHeader (undefined1[24]): Assembly-only temporary buffer used in disassembly,\n  not accessible for type refinement through decompiler interface (phantom variable)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x400: Path buffer size (1024 bytes)\n0x82: File header size (130 bytes)\n0xc0000000: GENERIC_READ | GENERIC_WRITE access flags\n0x8000000: FILE_FLAG_RANDOM_ACCESS\n0x3: OPEN_EXISTING\n0x18: Offset to flag field in file\n0x20: Persistence bit to set (0x20 = bit 5)\n\nFile Format:\nOffset 0x0: [0x82 bytes] - File header\nOffset 0x18: [4 bytes] - Flags (DWORD)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
