      "name": "OpenFileWithPermissions",
      "signature": "void * OpenFileWithPermissions(LPCSTR lpszFilePath, char * szMode, uint dwPermissions)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Opens a file with the specified path, mode, and permissions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire a file handle structure from the pool via FUN_6fdd7955\n2. If allocation fails, return NULL\n3. Parse mode string and open file via FUN_6fdd77e5\n4. Release the critical section lock via FUN_6fdd6f60\n5. Return the file pointer (or NULL on failure)\n\nParameters:\n- lpszFilePath (LPCSTR): Path to the file to open\n- szMode (char*): Mode string ('r', 'w', 'a', 'b', 't', '+' combinations)\n- dwPermissions (uint): Unix-style permissions (e.g., 0x1a4 = 0644)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to file structure on success, NULL on failure",
