      "name": "entry",
      "signature": "int entry(HMODULE hModule, int dwReason, void * lpvReserved)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "DLL entry point that manages module initialization, validation, and cleanup operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save original reason parameter for callback restoration\n2. Initialize result with global state from DAT_1003c8b0\n3. Handle process/thread attach (reason 1 or 2): call optional callback if available, then initialize module\n4. Validate Bink installation location for all entry reasons\n5. Handle process detach (reason 1): cleanup on validation failure, perform normal cleanup on success\n6. Handle process attach (reason 0) or thread detach (reason 3): perform additional cleanup operations\n7. Execute final callback if available and operation successful\n8. Return operation result or zero on failure\n\nParameters:\n  HMODULE hModule - Handle to the DLL module being loaded or unloaded\n  int dwReason - Reason for calling entry point (0=process attach, 1=process detach, 2=thread attach, 3=thread detach)\n  void* lpvReserved - Reserved parameter typically NULL for dynamic loads, non-NULL for static loads\n\nReturns:\n  int - Non-zero value indicates successful initialization/cleanup\n        Zero indicates failure (prevents DLL loading on attach, ignored on detach)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Callback function pointer at DAT_1003ce14 is optional and may be NULL\n  - Global state DAT_1003c8b0 affects initialization flow\n  - Process detach (reason 1) has special cleanup behavior on validation failure\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x0 - Process attach reason / NULL callback indicator\n  0x1 - Process detach reason\n  0x2 - Thread attach reason  \n  0x3 - Thread detach reason\n\nError Handling:\n  - Returns 0 immediately if callback returns 0 during attach operations\n  - Returns 0 if module initialization fails during attach\n  - Cleanup operations continue even if validation fails during detach",
