      "name": "AllocateStreamStructure",
      "signature": "void * AllocateStreamStructure(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocate and initialize a new stream structure slot from the global stream table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section lock (index 2) for global stream table access\n2. Iterate through all stream structure slots (0 to g_dwStreamStructureCount-1)\n3. For each slot:\n   a. Load pointer from g_pStreamStructureTable[nSlotIndex]\n   b. If pointer is NULL (empty slot found):\n      - Allocate 0x38 bytes of memory for new stream structure\n      - Store pointer in table\n      - If allocation successful:\n        * Initialize critical section at offset +0x20 within structure\n        * Enter critical section\n        * Zero-initialize structure fields (offsets 0, 4, 8, 12, 28)\n        * Set field at offset 16 (0x10) to 0xffffffff\n      - Break from loop\n   c. If pointer non-NULL, check OwningThread field (offset 0xc) bits [1:0] and [7:7]:\n      - If flags clear (flags & 0x83 == 0):\n        * Acquire critical section on existing slot\n        * Re-check flags after acquisition\n        * If still clear, zero-initialize structure fields (goto LAB_6fb9f238)\n        * Release critical section on failure/mismatch\n      - If flags set, continue to next slot\n4. Release critical section lock (index 2)\n5. Return pointer to allocated/initialized stream structure or NULL\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  Pointer to allocated and initialized stream structure (void *), or NULL if all slots occupied/allocation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Magic size 0x38 bytes for stream structure allocation\n  - Critical section at offset +0x20 within structure\n  - Field at offset +0x10 initialized to 0xffffffff (possibly busy/invalid flag)\n  - Reuses existing allocated slots if critical section not held\n  - Loops exit early on successful allocation or slot found\n\nStructure Layout (Stream Structure, 0x38 bytes):\n  Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n  0x00   | 4    | dwFieldZero | uint | Always initialized to 0\n  0x04   | 4    | dwFieldFour | uint | Always initialized to 0\n  0x08   | 4    | dwFieldEight | uint | Always initialized to 0\n  0x0c   | 1    | bFlags | byte | Flags (bits 0, 1, 7 significant)\n  0x10   | 4    | dwFieldSixteen | uint | Initialized to 0xffffffff (busy marker)\n  0x1c   | 4    | dwFieldTwentyEight | uint | Always initialized to 0\n  0x20+  | ~    | CriticalSection | CRITICAL_SECTION | Windows critical section structure",
