      "name": "McpClientJoinGamePollCallback",
      "signature": "uint McpClientJoinGamePollCallback(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "MCP Client Game Join Poll Callback\n\nCallback function invoked by MessagePumpLoop during game join sequence.\nPolls MCP client connection state and exits the message loop when the\njoin operation completes or is cancelled.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10003 (D2MCPCLIENT) - Poll/update MCP client state\n2. Call Ordinal_10031 (D2MCPCLIENT) - Check join operation status\n3. If status == 0 (in progress):\n   a. Call Ordinal_10002 (D2MCPCLIENT) - Check if connected\n   b. If connected AND g_fMcpCancelOperation == 0: Return 1 (continue polling)\n4. Call Ordinal_10030(0) (D2MCPCLIENT) - Disconnect/cleanup\n5. Call StopMessageLoop (D2WIN) - Exit message pump\n6. Return 1\n\nParameters: None (stdcall callback via MessagePumpLoop)\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Always returns 1 (TRUE)\n         Return value controls message loop continuation\n\nLocal Variables:\n  iVar1 (nStatus) - int - Return value from Ordinal_10031/10002 status checks\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_fMcpCancelOperation (0x6fa2189c) - Cancel flag set by user action\n\nCalled From:\n  FUN_6fa03f80 via MessagePumpLoop(McpClientJoinGamePollCallback)\n\nOrdinal Reference (D2MCPCLIENT.DLL):\n  Ordinal_10003 - Poll/update client state\n  Ordinal_10031 - Get join operation status (0 = in progress)\n  Ordinal_10002 - Check connection status (non-zero = connected)\n  Ordinal_10030 - Disconnect with error code parameter\n\nNote: Function body boundary is truncated in Ghidra (shows only 1 instruction).\nFull code visible in decompiler spans 0x6fa03f40-0x6fa03f72.",
