      "name": "ReleaseFileLockCallback",
      "signature": "void ReleaseFileLockCallback(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Exception cleanup callback that releases file locks during error handling.\n\nThis function is invoked by the C runtime exception handler to ensure file locks\nare properly released when fread encounters errors or exceptions. It accesses the\nFILE pointer from the exception handler's stack frame context rather than through\nstandard parameter passing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load FILE pointer from caller's stack frame at EBP+0x14\n2. Call __unlock_file to release the file lock\n3. Return to exception handler\n\nParameters:\n  pFile - FILE pointer (accessed via EBP+0x14 from exception handler context)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Cleanup operation with no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Uses __stdcall calling convention with callee stack cleanup\n  - Accesses FILE pointer indirectly through unaff_EBP+0x14 instead of parameter\n  - Designed to work within exception handling context where parameters are on stack\n  - Called by _fread's exception handler during error conditions",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:5f97d76a7bf7bad4437ec948fbad99b7",
