      "name": "SelectionSortPartition",
      "signature": "void SelectionSortPartition(byte * pArray, int elementSize, void * pCompareFunc)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Selection sort partitioning helper used by qsort implementation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if array has at least 2 elements (start < end), exit if not\n2. Initialize ESI to point to first element + element_size (next position)\n3. For each partition round (outer loop):\n   a. Initialize pMinElement to current array start position\n   b. Scan remaining elements (inner loop) calling comparison function\n   c. If comparison returns positive, update pMinElement pointer\n   d. After inner loop completes, check if minimum element differs from start\n   e. If different, swap minimum element with current position byte-by-byte\n   f. Move partition boundary down by element_size\n   g. Repeat until all elements partitioned\n4. Return to caller when partition complete\n\nParameters:\n- pArray (EAX): Pointer to array end (upper bound of partition range)\n- elementSize (EBP): Size of each array element in bytes\n- pCompareFunc ([ESP+0x24]): Function pointer to comparison function\n  Signature: int compare(byte *pElement1, byte *pElement2)\n  Returns: positive if pElement1 > pElement2, 0 or negative otherwise\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If elementSize is 0, no swap occurs even if minimum differs\n- Array traversal uses pointer arithmetic, not index calculation\n- Comparison function receives pointers to actual elements, not indices\n- Swap operation is byte-by-byte to handle arbitrary element sizes\n- Selection sort has O(n\u00b2) time complexity for n elements",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ffeaed223a7d62f7d52f1bb9b91b904d",
